diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e752cc4..fb7077e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,12 +1,15 @@
 # CadetCatch Search API
 
-Backend proof-of-concept for CadetCatch face search.
+AWS source patch and reference implementation for CadetCatch face search.
 
 This repo is intentionally separate from the iOS release worktree. It does not mutate App Store Connect, TestFlight, Cloudflare, AWS, DNS, or production by itself.
 
 ## Architecture
 
-- FastAPI exposes `/health`, `/admin/index-event`, `/search`, and `/event/{event_id}/stats`.
+- FastAPI preserves `/search` while adding a gateway-protected `/desktop/search` route.
+- A durable SQLite ingestion ledger records every source photo as queued, processing, indexed, skipped with a reason, or failed.
+- `POST /admin/photo-ingest` accepts signed upload notifications; `/admin/photo-ingest/reconcile` queues the existing source manifest.
+- `GET /search/status` reports actual index readiness and never equates process health with searchable photos.
 - Face embeddings are generated by `InsightFace` in production.
 - Qdrant stores face vectors in production.
 - Cloudflare R2 stores originals, thumbnails, and face crops in production.
@@ -87,3 +90,17 @@ docker compose up -d
 - Prefer private R2 objects with signed URLs.
 - Delete query uploads after processing.
 - Update app privacy policy and App Store privacy answers before shipping server-side face search.
+
+## Backfill and queue processing
+
+After configuring production secrets, Ken runs:
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST https://api.cadetcatch.com/admin/photo-ingest/reconcile \
+  -H "X-API-Key: $ADMIN_API_KEY"
+python scripts/process_ingest_queue.py --max-jobs 2500
+curl https://api.cadetcatch.com/admin/ingestion/status \
+  -H "X-API-Key: $ADMIN_API_KEY"
+```
+
+Re-running reconciliation is safe: source URLs are unique, SHA-256 identifies duplicate content, and deterministic vector point IDs make retries idempotent.
