+Install the durable queue timer:
+
+```bash
+sudo cp deploy/cadetcatch-ingestion-worker.service deploy/cadetcatch-ingestion-worker.timer /etc/systemd/system/
+sudo systemctl daemon-reload
+sudo systemctl enable --now cadetcatch-ingestion-worker.timer
+sudo systemctl list-timers cadetcatch-ingestion-worker.timer
+```
+
 ## Release Gates
 
 AWS instance creation, Cloudflare R2/DNS changes, and production deploy are release-sensitive external mutations for this EB28 workflow. They need explicit approval records before action.
+
+## Required production sequence
+
+1. Identify the exact currently deployed `/search` source and merge these changes there; do not point production at an unrelated proof-of-concept.
+2. Snapshot the vector store and ingestion database.
+3. Deploy the API with `/search` compatibility tests passing.
+4. Configure the upload portal HMAC secret and ingestion URL.
+5. Reconcile the source manifest, drain all jobs, and resolve every failure.
+6. Verify `/search/status` reports the expected source count and `ready: true`.
+7. Run a controlled upload and confirm it becomes searchable within five minutes with a self-search score of at least `0.99`.
+8. Only then switch the Cloudflare website from `WEB_ACCESS_MODE=closed` to `required`.
